  Benchmark family : EURAD-MS (EURAD-2 MS33 theoretical benchmarking, Model III)
  Geometry / BC    : axisymmetric clay cylinder r=23 mm (Ø46 mm), h=70 mm, inside the Ø50 mm
                     cell: 2 mm lateral technological gap represented by a BC SWITCH - the outer
                     radial boundary swells FREE until u_r reaches 2 mm (r = 25 mm = cell wall),
                     then becomes a rigid Dirichlet wall (container contact).
                     SPEC-CONFORMANCE FIX 2 (Vinay 2026-09-08 "approve all five, run them as one
                     campaign"; audits/2026-09-08_spec_conformance_full/AUDIT.md §3 + refutation
                     row 2): spec Fig3gapelementa.jpg labels the clay "46 mm" in the "50 mm" cell;
                     UCLM.tex L370 "radius of 23 mm"; CIMNE template row (23,0,40); CIMNE.tex L591
                     ~1.35 g/cm3 = 1600*(23/25)^2. Through gen 4 (2026-08-31) the clay was r = 25 mm
                     with the wall latched at r = 27 mm (effective Ø54 cell, +18 % clay volume,
                     post-closure rho_d 1372 vs the spec's 1354 kg/m3) - SUPERSEDED. Mesh: MaterialID 0
                     of the tracked ms33_gap2mm_r25_h70.vtu (1 x 1.75 mm, 920 quads) extracted as
                     ms33_clay_r23_h70.vtu; NOTE the discretisation is finer than the gen-4 5 x 5 mm
                     mesh (a refinement rides along with the geometry fix).  Switch implemented in
                     ms33_modelIII_gapswitch_bc.py (mirrors the Task-13 2023
                     getDirichletBCValue switch).  rho_d = 1600 kg/m3 at emplacement.

